    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "When the decision-maker who cast the roles chose the actor for the roles in his Homer adaptation, fierce online criticism erupted. Accusers attacking the production leveled an allegation of erasing European history, but those who stood up for the casting mounted a defense of inclusive storytelling. This defense statement argued that diverse casting treats the Western canon as shared civilizational heritage. The confrontation has turned the mythic epic into a cultural controversy, igniting a public dispute over who may claim classical stories in mass-market film.",
