    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "A digital backlash against the creative project saw public figures leading the charge against the production, making a public accusation of erasing European history. In the face of this digital backlash, protectors of diverse storytelling advanced a counter-argument. Their defense statement was a moral stance for inclusive representation. The battle over representation in film has now become a larger fight over cultural ownership, a societal debate playing out on the battleground where the fight plays out.",
